3. Ensure Table Keys Match in ProcessSummaryTableConfig.js
Finally, remember that the data feeding into your DynamicSummaryTable.jsx must perfectly match the field values defined in your config.
For example, if you click "SIBA", your data objects must contain the exact, case-sensitive keys: cgl, currency, and amount. If the backend sends { "CGL": "...", "Amount": 100 } (uppercase), the table will render blank cells because it's looking for the lowercase fields.
